---
import MotionFigure from '../relational-motion/MotionFigure.astro';
interface Props { kind: 'route' | 'prune' | 'keys' | 'retire'; }
const { kind } = Astro.props;
const titles = { route: 'One logical table, disjoint month ranges', prune: 'Which months can contain an answer?', keys: 'A unique pair does not make a unique order number', retire: 'Leaving the table is different from disappearing' };
const numbers = { route: 1, prune: 2, keys: 3, retire: 4 };
const months = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec'];
---
{kind === 'prune' || kind === 'retire' ? <MotionFigure collection="foundations/maintenance" kind={kind} number={numbers[kind]} /> : <figure class="partition-figure" data-partition-figure={kind} aria-labelledby={`partition-${kind}-title`}>
  <figcaption id={`partition-${kind}-title`}><span>Figure {numbers[kind]}</span> {titles[kind]}</figcaption>
  {kind === 'route' && <>
    <div class="scene route-scene">
      <div class="parent"><b>orders_monthly</b><small>Callers insert and query one table</small></div>
      <div class="arrow">placed_at selects one range ↓</div>
      <div class="range-pair">
        <div class="piece"><b>October</b><small>1 Oct ≤ placed_at &lt; 1 Nov</small><div class="record">103 · 20 Oct 10:15<br/>pending · customer 1</div><small>Order 103 belongs here.</small></div>
        <div class="piece"><b>November</b><small>1 Nov ≤ placed_at &lt; 1 Dec</small><div class="record boundary">Boundary probe<br/>1 Nov 00:00 UTC</div><small>The exact boundary belongs here.</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="server">One PostgreSQL instance contains both partitions and their indexes.</div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">Two of twelve monthly partitions. The November timestamp is a separate routing probe, not a new shop order. Lower bounds are included; upper bounds are excluded. These are table boundaries, not machine boundaries.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'prune' && <>
    <div class="options"><label>Query <select data-query aria-label="Query"><option value="october">October paid-order report</option><option value="year">Full-year paid-order report</option><option value="id">Order 103, with no time bound</option></select></label></div>
    <div class="scene">
      <p class="predicate" data-predicate data-live>1 Oct ≤ placed_at &lt; 1 Nov; status = paid</p>
      <div class="month-grid">{months.map((m, i) => <div class="month" data-month={i}><b>{m}</b><span data-month-state data-live>Candidate</span></div>)}</div>
      <p class="count" data-count data-live>12 candidate partitions</p>
      <div class="remaining"><b data-task-title data-live>Order work</b><p data-order-work data-live>First compare the query with the month bounds.</p><div class="join-work" data-line-work data-live>order_items remains a separate, unpartitioned table.</div></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The query names October's UTC range. Start with all twelve months.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="player" aria-label="Figure 2 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
    <p class="caption">A model of the pruning proof. “Kept” means the boundary cannot exclude the partition; it does not promise a scan method or a matching row. The line-table work remains visible after order pruning.</p>
    <details><summary>All queries and stages as text</summary><p>October: begin with twelve month ranges; exclude eleven disjoint ranges; test paid status within October; join eligible orders to lines and add by customer. Full year: all twelve ranges remain, then the same status, join and aggregation work is needed. ID only: the query gives no placed_at bound, so all twelve ranges remain possible; an index can search for 103 inside each. The ID lookup needs no order-line join.</p></details>
  </>}
  {kind === 'keys' && <>
    <div class="scene">
      <p class="predicate">PostgreSQL 18 · PRIMARY KEY (order_id, placed_at)</p>
      <div class="range-pair">
        <div class="piece"><b>October partition</b><div class="record">103<br/>20 Oct 10:15 UTC</div><small>First pair accepted.</small></div>
        <div class="piece"><b>November partition</b><div class="record boundary">103<br/>1 Nov 00:00 UTC</div><small>Different pair also accepted.</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="identity-result"><b>Same order number · different key pairs</b><p>The second 103 violates the shop's intended global identity, but not this composite key.</p></div>
      <div class="reference-line"><code>order_items.order_id → ?</code><p>103 alone no longer names one enforced parent key. A composite reference must carry and match placed_at too.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="caption">An isolated counterexample, not two valid purchases in the shop history. Repeating the exact October pair is rejected; repeating only the order number with a different time is accepted.</p>
  </>}
  {kind === 'retire' && <>
    <div class="options"><label>Approved cutoff <select data-cutoff aria-label="Approved cutoff"><option value="whole">1 February 2026, 00:00 UTC</option><option value="partial">15 January 2026, 00:00 UTC</option></select></label></div>
    <div class="scene">
      <div class="retirement-map"><div class="parent"><b>orders_monthly</b><div class="membership" data-membership data-live>January + February … December</div></div><div class="arrow" data-operation data-live>January is still attached ↓</div><div class="piece january"><b>January table</b><div class="jan-band"><span data-eligible data-live>All January rows eligible</span><span data-retained data-live></span></div><p data-exists data-live>Stored and reachable through the parent.</p></div></div>
      <div class="dependencies"><b>Related data and writers</b><p data-dependants data-live>Eligibility must cover each order and the related records in the approved scope.</p></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">The approved boundary is 1 February. Every timestamp in January lies before it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="player" aria-label="Figure 4 controls"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back aria-disabled="true">Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
    <p class="caption">A conceptual maintenance sequence after a hypothetical policy decision. Detachment leaves the table stored and directly queryable. Destruction is a later decision. The partial-month option stops before detachment because some January rows are still ineligible.</p>
    <details><summary>All retirement stages as text</summary><ol><li>Check every row against the approved cutoff. A 15 January cutoff leaves later January rows ineligible, so stop.</li><li>For the whole eligible month, resolve dependent records and incoming references; coordinate writers so the checked scope stays true.</li><li>Detach January. The parent now exposes February–December, while the January table still exists.</li><li>Where policy permits, verify the detached table and retain the agreed recovery stage under controlled access.</li><li>Drop it only when authorised, then verify the live result and track every remaining copy to its required outcome.</li></ol></details>
  </>}
</figure>}

<script>
  import { stepper } from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-partition-figure="prune"]').forEach(root => {
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-query]')!;
    const put = (selector: string, text: string) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent = text; };
    const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => 4, draw: (s: number) => {
      const mode = select.value;
      const oct = mode === 'october', id = mode === 'id';
      put('[data-predicate]', oct ? '1 Oct ≤ placed_at < 1 Nov; status = paid' : id ? 'order_id = 103; no placed_at bound' : '1 Jan 2026 ≤ placed_at < 1 Jan 2027; status = paid');
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-month]').forEach((cell, i) => {
        const excluded = s > 0 && oct && i !== 9;
        cell.classList.toggle('excluded', excluded);
        cell.classList.toggle('kept', s > 0 && !excluded);
        cell.querySelector('[data-month-state]')!.textContent = s === 0 ? 'Candidate' : excluded ? 'Excluded' : 'Kept';
      });
      put('[data-count]', s === 0 ? '12 candidate partitions' : oct ? '1 kept · 11 excluded by time' : '12 kept · 0 excluded by time');
      put('[data-order-work]', s === 0 ? 'First compare the query with the month bounds.' : s === 1 ? 'The boundary proof is complete. Work inside the kept partitions remains.' : id ? 'Search for order_id = 103 in each remaining partition; a local index can help.' : `Read eligible ${oct ? 'October' : '2026'} orders and test status = paid. Partitioning has not tested status.`);
      put('[data-line-work]', id ? 'This order-only lookup has no order-line join.' : s === 3 ? 'Join matching order IDs to order_items; add agreed line values by customer, then sort.' : 'order_items remains a separate, unpartitioned table.');
      const explanations = oct ? ["The query names October's UTC range. Start with all twelve months.", 'January–September and November–December cannot hold a timestamp in this range. Exclude them without testing their stored rows.', 'October can contain both paid and pending orders. It remains work: choose an access path and test paid status.', 'The surviving order IDs still need their lines. Pruning orders alone supplies no month boundary for the unpartitioned line table.'] : id ? ['103 identifies an order, but the query says nothing about when it was placed.', 'The month ranges constrain placed_at, not order_id. None proves that 103 is absent.', 'Local indexes may make each search cheap. They do not turn the ID predicate into a time predicate.', 'All twelve partitions remain candidates for this lookup. Supplying a trustworthy time bound could narrow that set.'] : ['The query asks for all of 2026. Start with the twelve monthly ranges.', 'Every month overlaps the requested year. No partition can be excluded by these time bounds.', 'The paid test still rejects pending orders inside every month.', 'The report still joins eligible orders to lines and adds their values. Twelve smaller pieces have not reduced the requested history.'];
      put('[data-explanation]', explanations[s]);
    }});
    select.addEventListener('change', () => player.render());
  });
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-partition-figure="retire"]').forEach(root => {
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-cutoff]')!;
    const put = (selector: string, text: string) => { root.querySelector(selector)!.textContent = text; };
    const player = stepper(root, { steps: () => select.value === 'whole' ? 5 : 2, draw: (s: number) => {
      const whole = select.value === 'whole';
      root.classList.toggle('partial', !whole);
      root.classList.toggle('detached', whole && s >= 2);
      root.classList.toggle('dropped', whole && s === 4);
      put('[data-eligible]', whole ? 'All January rows eligible' : 'Before 15 Jan · eligible');
      put('[data-retained]', whole ? '' : '15–31 Jan · retain');
      put('[data-membership]', whole && s >= 2 ? 'February … December' : 'January + February … December');
      put('[data-operation]', !whole && s > 0 ? 'STOP · month only partly eligible' : s < 2 ? 'January is still attached ↓' : s === 4 ? 'Detached January table dropped' : 'DETACH removes this membership');
      put('[data-exists]', whole && s === 4 ? 'Live table absent; other copies need their own outcome.' : whole && s >= 2 ? 'Still stored. Query January directly.' : 'Stored and reachable through the parent.');
      put('[data-dependants]', whole && s >= 1 ? 'Proceed only after dependent records and references are resolved and writers cannot recreate the retired scope.' : 'Eligibility must cover each order and the related records in the approved scope.');
      const text = whole ? ['The approved boundary is 1 February. Every timestamp in January lies before it.', 'Resolve order lines, payments and incoming references according to their own rules. Coordinate writers before treating the eligibility check as settled.', 'January leaves orders_monthly. A query of the parent no longer includes those rows; the detached table still holds them.', 'Where policy permits this stage, verify January directly and keep the agreed return path. Detachment alone has erased nothing.', 'After the authorised drop, verify the live result. Recovery copies, exports and derived records remain governed by their separate disposal plan.'] : ['A 15 January cutoff falls inside this partition. Only earlier January rows are eligible.', 'Stop: detaching January would also hide the later rows that must remain. Keep the month, remove eligible rows individually, or redesign the boundary through a checked change.'];
      put('[data-explanation]', text[s]);
    }});
    select.addEventListener('change', () => player.render());
  });
</script>

<style>
  .partition-figure { margin:2rem 0; font:.86rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
  figcaption { margin-bottom:.7rem; font:1.15rem/1.4 var(--font-serif); color:var(--color-text); }
  figcaption > span { margin-right:.65rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.09em; font:.65rem var(--font-mono); color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .scene { border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); background:var(--color-surface-alt); padding:1.2rem; }
  .parent { border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); padding:.7rem; text-align:center; background:var(--color-surface); }
  small { display:block; font:.76rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .arrow { text-align:center; margin:.7rem 0; font:.79rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  .range-pair { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; }
  .piece { border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); padding:.8rem; min-width:0; background:var(--color-surface); }
  .record { margin:.7rem 0; padding:.6rem; border-left:3px solid var(--teal); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 10%,var(--color-surface)); font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .boundary { border-color:var(--gold); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--gold) 10%,var(--color-surface)); }
  .server { margin-top:1rem; padding-top:.7rem; border-top:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary); font:.76rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  .options { margin-bottom:.8rem; }
  label { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.7rem; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  select,button { color:var(--color-text); background:var(--color-surface); border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); border-radius:3px; padding:.45rem .65rem; font:.78rem/1.4 var(--font-sans); max-width:100%; }
  select { flex:1; min-width:0; }
  button { cursor:pointer; }
  button[aria-disabled="true"] { color:var(--color-text-secondary); cursor:default; }
  :is(button,select,summary):focus-visible { outline:3px solid var(--color-accent); outline-offset:3px; }
  .predicate { font:.79rem/1.6 var(--font-mono); margin:0 0 1rem; }
  .month-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(6,minmax(0,1fr)); gap:.5rem; }
  .month { text-align:center; padding:.6rem .2rem; border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); background:var(--color-surface); }
  .month span { display:block; font:.65rem/1.5 var(--font-sans); }
  .month.excluded { border-style:dashed; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .month.excluded b { text-decoration:line-through; }
  .month.kept { box-shadow:inset 0 3px var(--teal); }
  .count { font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); margin:1rem 0; }
  .remaining,.dependencies,.reference-line { padding:.8rem; border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary); background:var(--color-surface); }
  .remaining p,.dependencies p,.reference-line p,.identity-result p { margin:.35rem 0 0; }
  .join-work { margin-top:.7rem; padding-top:.7rem; border-top:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .explanation { margin:1rem 0 0; border-left:3px solid var(--teal); padding-left:.8rem; min-height:4.8em; }
  .player { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.4rem; flex-wrap:wrap; padding:.75rem; border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); border-top:0; background:var(--color-surface); }
  [data-step] { margin-left:auto; font:.75rem var(--font-mono); }
  [data-hold] { width:100%; height:3px; background:var(--color-rule); }
  [data-hold] span { display:block; width:0; height:100%; background:var(--teal); }
  .caption { color:var(--color-text-secondary); font:.79rem/1.65 var(--font-sans); margin:.7rem 0; }
  details { font:.8rem/1.6 var(--font-sans); }
  summary { text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:.2em; cursor:pointer; }
  .identity-result { margin:1rem 0; padding:.8rem; border-left:3px solid var(--coral); }
  .dependencies { margin-top:1rem; }
  .jan-band { display:flex; margin:.7rem 0; }
  .jan-band span { flex:1; padding:.6rem; border:1px solid var(--teal); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--teal) 10%,var(--color-surface)); }
  .jan-band span:empty { display:none; }
  .partial .jan-band span:last-child { border-color:var(--gold); background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--gold) 10%,var(--color-surface)); }
  .january p { margin:.5rem 0 0; }
  .detached .january { border-style:dashed; }
  .dropped .january { background:var(--color-surface-alt); }
  .dropped .jan-band { text-decoration:line-through; }
  @media(max-width:500px) { .scene { padding:.8rem; } .range-pair { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:.7rem; } .month-grid { grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr)); } .player { gap:.35rem; } button { padding:.45rem .55rem; } }
</style>
